## Upstream attribution

This project is an independent implementation. Its user experience and some of
its behaviour are based on the open-source project Overlayed:

- Overlayed — https://github.com/overlayeddev/overlayed
- Copyright (C) Team Overlayed and Overlayed contributors
- License: GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE of that project)
- Commit referenced during research: ea02d23a9e786ea6e24c30be3d8a0af56c34ac17

Concepts whose behaviour was informed by that source, and which are therefore
covered by the AGPL attribution above:

- the Discord RPC authorization/authentication sequence and the set of
  per-channel event subscriptions,
- the participant mapping of Discord `voice_states` flags and the ordering rule
  (local user first, then case-insensitive nickname),
- the nine-anchor, DPI-clamped overlay placement model,
- click-through implemented as an ignored cursor event region.

All code in this repository was written for this project. No upstream source file
was copied verbatim. Details: docs/UPSTREAM_RESEARCH.md.

Discord Linux Overlay is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Team
Overlayed, and it is not a replacement for the Overlayed project.

